-- title:
--   The socle $\mathrm{Soc}(G)$ and direct products of nonabelian simple groups
-- statement:
--   A **minimal normal subgroup** of a group $G$ is a nontrivial normal subgroup $N$ such that every nontrivial normal subgroup of $G$ contained in $N$ equals $N$. The **socle** $\mathrm{Soc}(G)$ is the subgroup generated by all minimal normal subgroups; it is normal, and trivial for the trivial group.
--
--   A group is a **direct product of nonabelian simple groups** if it is isomorphic to $T_1\times\cdots\times T_k$ for some $k\ge0$ and simple groups $T_i$, none of them commutative ($k=0$ gives the trivial group).
--
--   When $\mathrm{srad}(K)=1$, the paper's series uses $S(K)=\mathrm{Soc}(K)$, which is then such a product (§9.2.1, p.94).
-- source:
--   Qiao, Zhang, Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), §3.5 (vi), p.20 (PDF p.24); §9.2.1, p.94 (PDF p.98)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace GroupIsoPoly

/-- A **minimal normal subgroup**: a nontrivial normal subgroup containing no smaller nontrivial
normal subgroup of the whole group. -/
def IsMinimalNormal {G : Type*} [Group G] (N : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  N.Normal ∧ N ≠ ⊥ ∧ ∀ M : Subgroup G, M.Normal → M ≠ ⊥ → M ≤ N → M = N

/-- **The socle** `Soc(G)`.

Qiao, Zhang, *Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order*, preprint,
Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), §3.5 (vi), p.20 (PDF p.24): "Socle: compute Soc(Q), the
subgroup generated by the minimal nontrivial normal subgroups of Q."

`soc G` is the subgroup generated by all minimal normal subgroups of `G`; it is `⊥` for the trivial
group. -/
def soc (G : Type*) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  sSup {N : Subgroup G | IsMinimalNormal N}

instance soc_normal (G : Type*) [Group G] : (soc G).Normal :=
  Subgroup.sSup_normal _ fun _ h => h.1

/-- **A direct product of nonabelian simple groups.**

Qiao, Zhang, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), §9.2.1, p.94 (PDF p.98): "set
S(K) = Soc(K), a direct product of nonabelian simple groups".

`IsProdNonabelianSimple G` says that `G` is isomorphic to a product `T₁ × ⋯ × T_k` of finitely many
simple groups, each noncommutative. The trivial group is the empty product (`k = 0`). -/
def IsProdNonabelianSimple (G : Type u) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ (k : ℕ) (T : Fin k → Type u) (_ : ∀ i, Group (T i)),
    (∀ i, IsSimpleGroup (T i) ∧ ∃ x y : T i, x * y ≠ y * x) ∧
      Nonempty (G ≃* ((i : Fin k) → T i))

end GroupIsoPoly


